+### 4.3 list_conversations
+
+A client asks for its own conversation summaries with `{"type":"list_conversations"}`. The optional `limit` is an integer from 1 through 200. The optional `before` cursor contains both an ISO `updatedAt` string and a `sessionId` string; malformed fields receive `INVALID_MESSAGE` even when history is disabled ([validated by: accepts the history request and rejects malformed limits and cursors](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L85)).
+
+| Field              | Type   | Required | Description                         |
+| ------------------ | ------ | -------- | ----------------------------------- |
+| `type`             | string | Yes      | `"list_conversations"`              |
+| `limit`            | number | No       | Page size, an integer from 1 to 200 |
+| `before.updatedAt` | string | No       | ISO activity time in the cursor     |
+| `before.sessionId` | string | No       | Session id breaking activity ties   |
+
+The server takes the user id from the authenticated WebSocket connection, ignores a `userId` in the frame, and passes `{limit, before}` to `SessionStore.listFor`. With `transport.history.enabled`, it answers on request with one `conversation_list` frame of newest-first summaries. Every summary contains only `sessionId`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, and `entryCount`, with both times as ISO strings; the client can page with the last row's cursor and reconnect to a selected id through `?sessionId=` when resume is enabled ([validated by: lists only the connected user’s metadata, pages with the wire cursor, and opens a selected conversation](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L114)).
+
+History is off by default. When it is off or the store has no `listFor`, the server answers `UNSUPPORTED` in an `error` frame rather than presenting an empty conversation list. The deployer opts into exposing this personal metadata to the authenticated client through `transport.history`, and the store's retention remains the deployer's responsibility (see re-cinq/HALEngine#41) ([validated by: refuses history when the deployer has not enabled it or the store cannot list](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L178)).
+
+A list request is answered outside the per-session turn lock, so an active stream does not delay the list and the list produces no `stream_end` ([validated by: answers a history request during a streaming turn without waiting for stream_end](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L191)).
+
 ## 5. Server-to-Client Messages
 
 ### 5.1 connected
@@ -357,6 +374,19 @@ Semantics:
 - The client SHOULD use this message to clear any "processing" or "loading" indicators.
 - The client MUST treat a run as complete only at `stream_end` or when the socket closes. Unparseable JSON is the one frame answered with `INVALID_FORMAT` and no `stream_end`, because the server cannot tell what it was meant to be; for it the client falls back on the socket closing.
 
+### 5.9 conversation_list
+
+The reply's `conversation_list` frame has `type` and `conversations` fields. Each row of `conversations` has `sessionId` (string), `createdAt` and `updatedAt` (ISO strings), and `entryCount` (number); it carries no conversation content ([validated by: lists only the connected user’s metadata, pages with the wire cursor, and opens a selected conversation](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L114)).
+
+| Field                       | Type     | Description                       |
+| --------------------------- | -------- | --------------------------------- |
+| `type`                      | string   | `"conversation_list"`             |
+| `conversations`             | array    | Newest-first summary rows         |
+| `conversations[].sessionId` | string   | Conversation id                   |
+| `conversations[].createdAt` | string   | ISO creation time                 |
+| `conversations[].updatedAt` | string   | ISO latest activity time          |
+| `conversations[].entryCount` | number   | Number of entries in conversation |
+
 ## 6. SessionEntry Objects
 
 A SessionEntry represents a single piece of content in the conversation. Every entry has a `role` field that determines its shape. The `role` acts as a discriminant for the union type.
diff --git a/src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts b/src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0f04205
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts
@@ -0,0 +1,223 @@
+import {once} from 'node:events';
+import type {AddressInfo} from 'node:net';
+import {WebSocket} from 'ws';
+import {createHalEngine} from '../config.js';
+import type {HalEngine} from '../config.js';
+import {InMemorySessionStore} from '../infrastructure/stores/inMemorySessionStore.js';
+import type {SessionListOptions, SessionSummary} from '../types/sessionStore.js';
+import {validateMessage} from './ws/validation.js';
+import {HAL_WS_SUBPROTOCOL} from './ws/subprotocol.js';
+
+interface Frame {
+  type: string;
+  code?: string;
+  message?: string;
+  sessionId?: string;
+  resumed?: boolean;
+  conversations?: Array<Omit<SessionSummary, 'createdAt' | 'updatedAt'> & {createdAt: string; updatedAt: string}>;
+}
+
+class RecordingStore extends InMemorySessionStore {
+  calls: Array<{userId: string | number; options?: SessionListOptions}> = [];
+
+  override listFor(userId: string | number, options?: SessionListOptions): SessionSummary[] {
+    this.calls.push({userId, options});
+    return super.listFor(userId, options);
+  }
+}
+
+const engines: HalEngine[] = [];
+const clients: WebSocket[] = [];
+
+afterEach(async () => {
+  const closed = clients.splice(0).map(client => {
+    if (client.readyState === WebSocket.CLOSED) return Promise.resolve();
+    const finished = once(client, 'close');
+    client.terminate();
+    return finished;
+  });
+  await Promise.all(closed);
+  for (const engine of engines.splice(0)) await engine.stop();
+});
+
+async function start(
+  store: InMemorySessionStore,
+  history?: {enabled: boolean},
+  beforeModelResponse?: () => Promise<string>
+): Promise<string> {
+  const engine = createHalEngine({
+    provider: {type: 'mock'},
+    prompt: {identity: 'Test assistant'},
+    session: store,
+    auth: {ws: async () => ({id: 'owner'})},
+    orchestrator: beforeModelResponse ? {hooks: {beforeModelResponse}} : undefined,
+    transport: {
+      resume: {enabled: true},
+      ...({history} as object),
+    },
+  });
+  engines.push(engine);
+  await engine.start(0);
+  const {port} = engine.server.address() as AddressInfo;
+  return `ws://127.0.0.1:${port}/hal/ws`;
+}
+
+function connect(url: string): WebSocket {
+  const client = new WebSocket(url, [HAL_WS_SUBPROTOCOL, 'token']);
+  clients.push(client);
+  return client;
+}
+
+async function ask(url: string, request: object): Promise<{connected: Frame; answer: Frame; client: WebSocket}> {
+  const client = connect(url);
+  const connected = new Promise<Frame>(resolve => {
+    client.once('message', raw => resolve(JSON.parse(String(raw)) as Frame));
+  });
+  const first = await connected;
+  const answer = new Promise<Frame>(resolve => {
+    client.once('message', raw => resolve(JSON.parse(String(raw)) as Frame));
+  });
+  client.send(JSON.stringify(request));
+  return {connected: first, answer: await answer, client};
+}
+
+// specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md#1
+it('accepts the history request and rejects malformed limits and cursors', () => {
+  expect(validateMessage({type: 'list_conversations'})).toEqual({valid: true, data: {type: 'list_conversations'}});
+  for (const limit of [0, 201, 1.5, '10']) {
+    expect(validateMessage({type: 'list_conversations', limit})).toMatchObject({
+      valid: false,
+      error: expect.stringMatching(/limit/),
+    });
+  }
+  for (const before of [
+    'not a date',
+    {updatedAt: 'not a date', sessionId: 's1'},
+    {updatedAt: '2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z'},
+    {sessionId: 's1'},
+  ]) {
+    expect(validateMessage({type: 'list_conversations', before})).toMatchObject({
+      valid: false,
+      error: expect.stringMatching(/before/),
+    });
+  }
+  expect(
+    validateMessage({
+      type: 'list_conversations',
+      limit: 1,
+      before: {updatedAt: '2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z', sessionId: 's1'},
+    })
+  ).toMatchObject({valid: true});
+});
+
+// specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md#2
+it('lists only the connected user’s metadata, pages with the wire cursor, and opens a selected conversation', async () => {
+  const store = new RecordingStore();
+  store
+    .create('older', 'owner')
+    .entries.push({role: 'user', content: 'older content', timestamp: '2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z'});
+  store
+    .create('newer', 'owner')
+    .entries.push({role: 'user', content: 'newer content', timestamp: '2026-02-01T00:00:00.000Z'});
+  store
+    .create('someone-else', 'another-user')
+    .entries.push({role: 'user', content: 'private content', timestamp: '2026-03-01T00:00:00.000Z'});
+  const url = await start(store, {enabled: true});
+
+  const {connected, answer, client} = await ask(url, {type: 'list_conversations', userId: 'another-user'});
+  expect(answer.type).toBe('conversation_list');
+  expect(answer.conversations).toHaveLength(3);
+  expect(answer.conversations?.map(row => row.sessionId)).toEqual([connected.sessionId, 'newer', 'older']);
+  for (const row of answer.conversations ?? []) {
+    expect(Object.keys(row).sort()).toEqual(['createdAt', 'entryCount', 'sessionId', 'updatedAt']);
+    expect(row.createdAt).toBe(new Date(row.createdAt).toISOString());
+    expect(row.updatedAt).toBe(new Date(row.updatedAt).toISOString());
+  }
+  expect(store.calls[0]).toEqual({userId: 'owner', options: {limit: undefined, before: undefined}});
+
+  const settled: Frame[] = [];
+  const pong = new Promise<void>(resolve => {
+    const receive = (raw: Buffer) => {
+      const frame = JSON.parse(String(raw)) as Frame;
+      settled.push(frame);
+      if (frame.type === 'pong') {
+        client.off('message', receive);
+        resolve();
+      }
+    };
+    client.on('message', receive);
+  });
+  client.send(JSON.stringify({type: 'ping', timestamp: 1}));
+  await pong;
+  expect(settled.map(frame => frame.type)).toEqual(['pong']);
+
+  const cursor = {updatedAt: answer.conversations![0].updatedAt, sessionId: answer.conversations![0].sessionId};
+  const paged = new Promise<Frame>(resolve => client.once('message', raw => resolve(JSON.parse(String(raw)) as Frame)));
+  client.send(JSON.stringify({type: 'list_conversations', limit: 1, before: cursor}));
+  const page = await paged;
+  expect(page.conversations?.map(row => row.sessionId)).toEqual(['newer']);
+  expect(store.calls[1]).toEqual({userId: 'owner', options: {limit: 1, before: cursor}});
+
+  client.close();
+  await once(client, 'close');
+  const reopened = connect(`${url}?sessionId=newer`);
+  const replay: Frame[] = [];
+  await new Promise<void>(resolve => {
+    reopened.on('message', raw => {
+      const frame = JSON.parse(String(raw)) as Frame;
+      replay.push(frame);
+      if (frame.type === 'connected') reopened.send(JSON.stringify({type: 'ping', timestamp: 1}));
+      if (frame.type === 'pong') resolve();
+    });
+  });
+  expect(replay[0]).toMatchObject({type: 'connected', sessionId: 'newer', resumed: true});
+  expect(replay.some(frame => frame.type === 'entry_upsert')).toBe(true);
+});
+
+// specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md#3
+it('refuses history when the deployer has not enabled it or the store cannot list', async () => {
+  const disabled = await start(new InMemorySessionStore());
+  const first = await ask(disabled, {type: 'list_conversations'});
+  expect(first.answer).toMatchObject({type: 'error', code: 'UNSUPPORTED'});
+
+  const store = new InMemorySessionStore();
+  Object.defineProperty(store, 'listFor', {value: undefined});
+  const enabled = await start(store, {enabled: true});
+  const second = await ask(enabled, {type: 'list_conversations'});
+  expect(second.answer).toMatchObject({type: 'error', code: 'UNSUPPORTED'});
+});
+
+// specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md#4
+it('answers a history request during a streaming turn without waiting for stream_end', async () => {
+  let entered!: () => void;
+  let release!: () => void;
+  const inModel = new Promise<void>(resolve => {
+    entered = resolve;
+  });
+  const held = new Promise<void>(resolve => {
+    release = resolve;
+  });
+  const url = await start(new InMemorySessionStore(), {enabled: true}, async () => {
+    entered();
+    await held;
+    return 'Test assistant';
+  });
+  const client = connect(url);
+  const frames: Frame[] = [];
+  const reply = new Promise<Frame>(resolve => {
+    client.on('message', raw => {
+      const frame = JSON.parse(String(raw)) as Frame;
+      frames.push(frame);
+      if (frame.type === 'connected') client.send(JSON.stringify({type: 'user_message', content: 'hello'}));
+      if (frame.type === 'conversation_list' || frame.type === 'error') resolve(frame);
+    });
+  });
+  try {
+    await inModel;
+    client.send(JSON.stringify({type: 'list_conversations'}));
+    expect((await reply).type).toBe('conversation_list');
+    expect(frames.some(frame => frame.type === 'stream_end')).toBe(false);
+  } finally {
+    release();
+  }
+});